{
  "name": "step3-holdout-folds",
  "notes": "STEP 3 of the three-step data selection (ADR-0222): lock the holdout, admit the feature families, and cut the rolling-origin fold table. Input is step 2's dates.jsonl (onboarded through source-step2-dates.json) plus the same prepared panel as steps 1-2, read only for each cohort date's settlement_date. Order is the point: (1) holdout-cut locks the last 20% of the cohort's dates and purges dev rows whose label reaches it; (2) a family is admitted when available on >= tau (0.9) of dev dates, and the complete-case dates (every admitted family available) are the dates the folds are SIZED by; (3) rolling-origin-plan windows those dates into folds (train_n 450, val_n 40, step_n 40, the oldest warmup_folds 4 marked warmup, the rest scored) with the embargo equal to the selected DTE. Outputs in pipeline_runs/step3-holdout-folds: fold-table.jsonl (the fold table) and admission-and-metrics.jsonl (admitted families, holdout and plan metrics). No training-dates file is written (a writer that runs before the plan could leave a stale file behind a refused run). A fold carries only its boundary dates and counts, and steps 4-6 slice EVERY panel row between those boundaries, so a date missing an admitted family (about 8% of QQQ dev dates) is median-imputed there, not excluded, and a fold's train_dates and val_dates count only the complete-case dates, so its window can span more panel dates than the count. Owner decision 2026-10-02 (option A): median imputation is ACCEPTED and no complete-case filter will be built. The knob values are derived in ADR-0222 from the committed QQQ rows and carried in each node's notes; nothing derivable is typed (embargo, holdout_start, tickers, dates). Selection in steps 4-6 uses warmup folds only and must drop every warm-up validation row whose label reaches plan.scored_start. Memory: the source and the panel are each read once; every other node holds at most one ticker's dates.",
  "pipeline": {
    "step2_dates": {
      "uses": "dskit.pipeline.libs.observations:ObservationRows",
      "params": {
        "root": "./pipeline_runs/step2-dates-source",
        "source": "step2-dates",
        "stream": "dates",
        "key_fields": [
          "symbol",
          "quote_date"
        ],
        "ts_field": "quote_date",
        "ts_unit": "iso",
        "ts_out": "quote_date_ms"
      },
      "notes": "Step 2's dates.jsonl onboarded through source-step2-dates.json, the way step 2 reads step 1's selected.jsonl: one row per cohort date and ticker with the 13 available_<family> yes/no flags and the selected actual_calendar_dte. key_fields is (symbol, quote_date) because step 2 refuses a date with two availability patterns, so a duplicate key here means the file was edited. ts_field is quote_date (ISO), not the ADR's asof_ms: these rows carry no asof_ms, and ts_out quote_date_ms is free because they carry no such field either. Use a fresh onboarding root whenever step 2 is re-run: acquired data is immutable."
    },
    "source": {
      "uses": "dskit.pipeline.libs.observations:ObservationRows",
      "params": {
        "root": "/home/russell/data/index_options/ob",
        "source": "cdf-horizon-panel",
        "stream": "input_panel",
        "key_fields": [
          "symbol",
          "quote_date",
          "expiry"
        ],
        "ts_field": "quote_date",
        "ts_unit": "iso",
        "ts_out": "quote_date_ms"
      },
      "notes": "The SAME prepared option panel steps 1-2 read, read here for ONE column step 2's dates.jsonl does not carry: settlement_date, the day each date's label is known (the holdout purge and the embargo need it as end_field). Only dates already in step 2's cohort are looked up from it; no panel row becomes a cohort row. Another panel changes only these params, exactly as in steps 1-2. Root is the onboarding store (source cdf-horizon-panel, stream input_panel), not a per-run copy."
    },
    "columns": {
      "uses": "concat",
      "params": {
        "shape": "table",
        "tables": {
          "columns": {
            "date_field": "quote_date",
            "end_field": "settlement_date"
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": "The two column names holdout-cut and rolling-origin-plan must agree on, declared ONCE and referenced by both ($columns.merged.date_field / end_field), so the cut and the folds can never read different dates. date_field is the cohort date (entry day). end_field is settlement_date, the day the label is known: on all QQQ rows it is 7 days after the entry date, while expiry is 8-9 days out on 42 rows and would exceed the 7-day embargo and refuse (ADR-0222)."
    },
    "tau": {
      "uses": "concat",
      "params": {
        "shape": "table",
        "tables": {
          "admission": {
            "tau": 0.9
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": "tau, the family admission threshold, declared ONCE; every admit_<family> derive reads it ($tau.merged.tau). A family is admitted when it is available on at least tau of the pre-holdout dates. 0.9 admits 6 of the 13 (counting family flags only; the four aggregate available_core* flags are not families) families on the committed QQQ rows and leaves 1,096 complete-case dev dates (ADR-0222); judgment the owner may override. Gaps are assumed random for now, though surface gaps cluster in 2011-2014."
    },
    "fold_rows": {
      "uses": "concat",
      "inputs": {
        "fold_table__each": "$fold_table.records"
      },
      "params": {
        "shape": "records",
        "key": "symbol",
        "provenance_waiver": "each fold row carries its own symbol (the fold_table derive stamps it); the key check proves no ticker appears twice"
      }
    },
    "fold_evidence": {
      "uses": "records-write",
      "inputs": {
        "records": "$fold_rows.merged"
      },
      "params": {
        "path": "./pipeline_runs/step3-holdout-folds/fold-table.jsonl",
        "source": "The fold table: one row per rolling-origin fold and ticker (fold, role warmup|scored, train/val start and end, date and ISO-week counts, purged), oldest first. Pin it by provenance.sha256 (metrics.sha256) and holdout_start by value; never re-cut it."
      },
      "notes": "Refuses to overwrite and needs its parent directory: mkdir -p pipeline_runs/step3-holdout-folds, and move that directory aside to repeat. With more than one ticker the file holds one fold-id series per ticker and each ticker has its own holdout_start, so the study's fold_table reader (unique fold ids, one holdout_start) refuses it: for a study, run with ONE foreach key (a copy of this file differing only there) and a fresh output directory."
    },
    "admission_rows": {
      "uses": "concat",
      "inputs": {
        "protocol__each": "$protocol.records"
      },
      "params": {
        "shape": "records",
        "key": "symbol",
        "provenance_waiver": "each row carries its own symbol; the key check proves no ticker appears twice"
      }
    },
    "admission_evidence": {
      "uses": "records-write",
      "inputs": {
        "records": "$admission_rows.merged"
      },
      "params": {
        "path": "./pipeline_runs/step3-holdout-folds/admission-and-metrics.jsonl",
        "source": "One row per ticker: dev_dates, rate_<f> (share of dev dates on which family f is available), required_<f> (1 = admitted at tau), holdout (holdout-cut metrics: holdout_start, holdout_end, holdout_dates, holdout_weeks, dev_dates, purged_rows, holdout_rows, panel_rows) and plan (rolling-origin-plan metrics: folds, scored, warmup_weeks, scored_start)"
      },
      "notes": "The persisted handoff values: a consumer reads holdout.holdout_start and plan.scored_start BY VALUE from here and never recomputes them (a fraction cut and an end-anchored grid both move when dates are appended). Same overwrite and parent-directory rules as fold_evidence."
    }
  },
  "outputs": {
    "run_root": "./pipeline_runs/step3-holdout-folds/runs"
  },
  "foreach": {
    "keys": [
      "QQQ"
    ],
    "notes": "One ticker per run: the study's fold_table reader needs unique fold ids and one holdout_start, so run step 3 once per ticker (set keys to that ticker) into a fresh output directory, then point that ticker's study config at its fold table.",
    "pipeline": {
      "ticker_dates": {
        "uses": "filter",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$step2_dates.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "where": [
            {
              "field": "symbol",
              "op": "==",
              "value": "$each"
            }
          ]
        },
        "notes": "This ticker's step-2 cohort dates. An empty result (a ticker step 2 never ran) leaves dte without an 'all' key and the run refuses at settled, the first node to read it."
      },
      "dte_groups": {
        "uses": "groupby",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$ticker_dates.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "keys": [
            "selection_group",
            "actual_calendar_dte"
          ],
          "aggregates": {
            "rows": {
              "op": "count"
            }
          }
        },
        "notes": "One row per distinct DTE in the cohort: step 2 filtered to step 1's selected DTE, so there is exactly one. The keyby below refuses a second one."
      },
      "dte": {
        "uses": "keyby",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$dte_groups.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "key": "selection_group",
          "value": "actual_calendar_dte"
        },
        "notes": "The embargo, read from the rows' own actual_calendar_dte, which step 2 pinned to step 1's selected DTE (its agreed_dte refusal): never typed. keyby refuses a repeated key, so two DTEs in one cohort refuse instead of picking one. Calendar days to settlement is the lifetime of every label, so no label can outlive it."
      },
      "settled": {
        "uses": "filter",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$source.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "where": [
            {
              "field": "symbol",
              "op": "==",
              "value": "$each"
            },
            {
              "field": "actual_calendar_dte",
              "op": "==",
              "value": "$dte.table.all"
            },
            {
              "field": "terminal_return",
              "op": "!=",
              "value": null
            },
            {
              "field": "settlement_date",
              "op": "!=",
              "value": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "notes": "The panel rows at the cohort's DTE whose label is known (step 2's own terminal_return != null rule), kept only to read settlement_date."
      },
      "settlement_groups": {
        "uses": "groupby",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$settled.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "keys": [
            "symbol",
            "quote_date",
            "settlement_date"
          ],
          "aggregates": {
            "rows": {
              "op": "count"
            }
          }
        },
        "notes": "One row per (date, settlement date): expiries on one date collapse here, and a date with two settlement dates yields two rows, which settlement_by_date refuses."
      },
      "settlement_by_date": {
        "uses": "keyby",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$settlement_groups.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "key": "quote_date",
          "value": "settlement_date"
        },
        "notes": "quote_date -> settlement_date. A date with two different settlement dates would make its label end ambiguous, so keyby refuses the repeated key."
      },
      "dated": {
        "uses": "join",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$ticker_dates.records",
          "settlement_date": "$settlement_by_date.table"
        },
        "params": {
          "key": "quote_date",
          "how": "strict"
        },
        "notes": "Adds settlement_date to every cohort date. strict: a cohort date with no panel row at that DTE refuses naming the date, so the source or ticker changing between steps 2 and 3 cannot go unnoticed. This is the only join; step 2's rows lack the column and the kinds need it as end_field."
      },
      "cut": {
        "uses": "holdout-cut",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$dated.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "date_field": "$columns.merged.date_field",
          "end_field": "$columns.merged.end_field",
          "fraction": 0.2
        },
        "notes": "Holdout FIRST, on the full cohort: the last ceil(0.2 x dates) dates are locked and only dev rows (dates before the holdout whose label settles before holdout_start) and dates-only metrics leave this node. fraction 0.2 (the owner's H) is 300 holdout dates, about 66 weeks, on the committed QQQ rows (1,497 dates); C4 needs at least 52 weeks, one annual cycle. Every node after this one reads $cut.records, never $dated, so nothing downstream can see a holdout row."
      },
      "has_implied_cdf": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$cut.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_implied_cdf",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_implied_cdf",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_implied_cdf",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        },
        "notes": "has_<family>: step 2 writes each family's availability as the strings yes/no, and groupby mean needs numbers, so each family gets a 0/1 twin. Chained, one derive per family; derive is fail-closed, so any value other than yes/no (a step-2 vocabulary change) refuses instead of counting as 0. Dev rows only: the chain starts at $cut.records."
      },
      "has_return_history": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_implied_cdf.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_return_history",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_return_history",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_return_history",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_realized_volatility": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_return_history.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_realized_volatility",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_realized_volatility",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_realized_volatility",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_ohlc_shape": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_realized_volatility.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_ohlc_shape",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_ohlc_shape",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_ohlc_shape",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_volatility_context": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_ohlc_shape.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_volatility_context",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_volatility_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_volatility_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_expanded_volatility_context": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_volatility_context.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_expanded_volatility_context",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_expanded_volatility_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_expanded_volatility_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_surface_level": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_expanded_volatility_context.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_surface_level",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_surface_level",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_surface_level",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_surface_changes": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_surface_level.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_surface_changes",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_surface_changes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_surface_changes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_variance_gap": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_surface_changes.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_variance_gap",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_variance_gap",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_variance_gap",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_liquidity": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_variance_gap.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_liquidity",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_liquidity",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_liquidity",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_positioning_changes": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_liquidity.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_positioning_changes",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_positioning_changes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_positioning_changes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_macro_context": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_positioning_changes.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_macro_context",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_macro_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_macro_context",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "has_chain_nodes": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_macro_context.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "has_chain_nodes",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_chain_nodes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "yes"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "available_chain_nodes",
                  "op": "==",
                  "value": "no"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "admission": {
        "uses": "groupby",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$has_chain_nodes.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "keys": [
            "symbol",
            "selection_group"
          ],
          "aggregates": {
            "dev_dates": {
              "op": "count"
            },
            "rate_implied_cdf": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_implied_cdf"
            },
            "rate_return_history": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_return_history"
            },
            "rate_realized_volatility": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_realized_volatility"
            },
            "rate_ohlc_shape": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_ohlc_shape"
            },
            "rate_volatility_context": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_volatility_context"
            },
            "rate_expanded_volatility_context": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_expanded_volatility_context"
            },
            "rate_surface_level": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_surface_level"
            },
            "rate_surface_changes": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_surface_changes"
            },
            "rate_variance_gap": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_variance_gap"
            },
            "rate_liquidity": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_liquidity"
            },
            "rate_positioning_changes": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_positioning_changes"
            },
            "rate_macro_context": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_macro_context"
            },
            "rate_chain_nodes": {
              "op": "mean",
              "field": "has_chain_nodes"
            }
          }
        },
        "notes": "The mean of each 0/1 flag over the PRE-HOLDOUT dates only (one row per ticker): the share of dev dates on which the family is available. The holdout never enters the admission, so which families train cannot depend on it."
      },
      "admit_implied_cdf": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$admission.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "required_implied_cdf",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "rate_implied_cdf",
                  "op": ">=",
                  "value": "$tau.merged.tau"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "rate_implied_cdf",
                  "op": "<",
                  "value": "$tau.merged.tau"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        },
        "notes": "required_<family> = 1 when the family's dev availability rate is >= tau (declared once in the tau node), else 0. Admitted means required: a training date must have the family. Chained, one derive per family. Both outcomes are explicit cases, so an unorderable rate refuses."
      },
      "admit_return_history": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$admit_implied_cdf.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "required_return_history",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "rate_return_history",
                  "op": ">=",
                  "value": "$tau.merged.tau"
                }
              ],
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "rate_return_history",
                  "op": "<",
                  "value": "$tau.merged.tau"
                }
              ],
              "value": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "admit_realized_volatility": {
        "uses": "derive",
        "inputs": {
          "records": "$admit_return_history.records"
        },
        "params": {
          "field": "required_realized_volatility",
          "cases": [
            {
              "when": [
                {
                  "field": "rate_realized_volatility",
